  <note id="note0" x="-76" y="66" color="#fff3b0" text="IP telephony: phones register with the call manager, and a call is just software between two extensions. The phone ports are trunks: data rides VLAN 1 untagged and the voice VLAN 110 is tagged, with OfficeRouter's Gig0/0.110 subinterface as the voice gateway. Each desk phone also draws its power over the cable (PoE, IEEE 802.3af) — power inline never on its port shuts the phone down. Try: open either phone's window and place the call, then check the other phone rings."/>
